infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The __eq__/__hash__ contract: define both, or lose hashing
  desc Equal objects must hash equal — so defining __eq__ without __hash__ makes instances unhashable
  compares
    - label correct
      children
        - label Define __eq__ AND __hash__
          desc Hash the same fields you compare
        - label Equal objects hash equal
          desc The invariant dicts and sets rely on
        - label Instances stay hashable
          desc Usable as set members and dict keys
        - label Keep hashed fields immutable
          desc Else x in s goes False while x sits in s
    - label trap
      children
        - label Define __eq__ alone
          desc No __hash__ to match your equality
        - label Python sets __hash__ = None
          desc It cannot guarantee equal objects hash equal
        - label Instances become unhashable
          desc Nothing fails at class-definition time
        - label Crashes at first set/dict use
          desc TypeError in the 3 a.m. job, far from your diff
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
